# Agent C - Shared Memory Injection Log

Status: complete

Subagent: Ohm.

Findings:

- React Shared Memory Hub could create/search/archive, but generation passed `undefined` into `generateSharedMemoryContext`.
- React Prompt Lab had a separate toggle and no real stored-memory array in automatic injection.
- Static Prompt Lab lacked `off` mode and always prefixed memory context.
- Static Shared Memory lacked search and archive/restore actions.

Implemented:

- Prompt Lab now uses one off/minimal/balanced/full option set with localized labels.
- React Prompt Lab loads memories and injects a real memory array.
- Project Detail injects project-scoped memory arrays instead of a project id string.
- SharedMemoryHub recovery prompt now includes project name, current scheme, launch method, known limitation, next step, and canonical context.
- Static Shared Memory adds search and archive/restore.
- Static Prompt Lab supports `off`, `minimal`, `balanced`, and `full`.
- Context marker is canonical `[Shared Memory Context] ... [/Shared Memory Context]`.

Verification:

- `npm.cmd run smoke`: PASS.
- `npm.cmd run test:launch-static`: PASS.
